The Word file and the browser copy stop disagreeing

Five of the six things that came back from the Kevin Truong agreement.
Four of them were the same fault: the DOCX builder and the stylesheet
each deciding for themselves, and quietly differing.

The firm profile printed between the cover and the client's own letter in
Word, and at the back in the browser. body() is asked for the agreement
without the letterhead, and the profile rides with the letterhead, so
this builder added its own copy and added it early. It now goes where the
browser already put it: after the signatures and the payment page.

The body was justified in the browser and left-aligned in Word, because
the stylesheet says `text-align:justify` and the builder emitted no w:jc
at all. The file JJ sent back had 0 justified paragraphs out of 164; it
now has 88 out of 167, with the headings left alone.

The offices were printed three times: on the letterhead, in the profile,
and in a footer of their own. Three places to correct when an office
moves. The footer is gone and its styles with it.

The print button was href="javascript:window.print()". Chrome does not
mind. Safari treats following one as a navigation, begins replacing the
document, and prints the replacement: the copy JJ sent was a single blank
letter page, 901 bytes, Creator "Safari". It is a button now, wired by
public/print-view.js, and the same pattern is fixed in app-api.js and in
audit-ui.js's two receipts.

The payment page was not broken. It prints the account details whenever
they are configured -- it does so on the M1, where the local file exists
-- and falls back to "telephone the office" when they are not. The fault
is that it fell back SILENTLY, so an agreement went out with no wire
instructions and nobody knew. The review page now says so in red before
the agreement is sent, and names the TEZ_PAY_* variables still to set. No
values in the page and none in the log.

Still open, and needing a decision rather than a fix: sending for
signature asks for an upload because createDraft() wants a PDF buffer and
the server cannot make one -- no headless browser on Render, no CJK font
in the repo, and pdf-lib's built-in fonts are Latin-1 only.

13 checks. Also removes .commitmsg, which a `git add -A` committed in
8cedc64, and gitignores it.

